  "reason": "The best configuration so far is config_037 (scgpt, imagenet_vit_l, avgpool, weighted) at 0.542 accuracy. The strongest evidence shows multiprofile + avgpool + weighted fusion + imagenet_vit_l is the optimal architecture. However, the RNA encoder (scgpt) has only been tested in this best setup; scvi_n200, a learned variational embedding, remains untested in this exact configuration. Config_046 (scvi_n200, imagenet_vit_l, avgpool, weighted) directly tests whether an alternative RNA encoder can match or exceed scgpt in the best-performing architecture. This is the highest-value single-variable change: if scvi_n200 performs comparably, it confirms the architecture is the bottleneck; if it exceeds scgpt, we find a new best. With only 1 experiment remaining after this, testing the most impactful untested variable (RNA encoder) in the proven best setup is the best use of the budget to either improve on 0.542 or confirm the ceiling."
